    "id": "C1",
    "text": "urllib.parse.urlparse splits a URL with semicolon-delimited path parameters into .path and .params attributes.",
    "source_quote": "When a URL contains path parameters delimited by semicolons (e.g. `https://musicbrainz.org/ws/2/artist;name=Nirvana`), `urllib.parse.urlparse` splits the path into `.path` and `.params` attributes.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "same"
   },
   {
    "id": "C2",
    "text": "Before the fix, HTTPDigestAuth.build_digest_header() used only .path and .query, causing the uri field in the Authorization header to be truncated.",
    "source_quote": "`HTTPDigestAuth.build_digest_header()` was only using `.path` and `.query`, so the `uri` field in the `Authorization` header was truncated, causing authentication to fail on servers that validate the full request URI.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "same"
   },
   {
    "id": "C3",
    "text": "After the fix, HTTPDigestAuth.build_digest_header() includes p_parsed.params when reconstructing the path, so the uri field contains semicolon-delimited path parameters.",
    "source_quote": "Fix: include `p_parsed.params` when reconstructing the path in `build_digest_header()`.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   }
